$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for catalytic hydrogenation
The solution of the starting compound (10.0 mmol) in appropriate solvent
in the presence of palladium on activated charcoal (10 % by weight) was
stirred under hydrogen atmosphere overnight. The product was isolated by
filtration and evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure.
4-[(7-Amino-3-oxo-2,3-dihydro-4H-1,4-benzoxazin-4-yl)methyl]benzonitrile
(4) 7. Synthesis of ethyl
2-({3-[(4-{4-[amino(imino)methyl]benzyl}-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-
yl)amino]-2-benzyl-3-oxopropanoyl}amino)acetate acetate (10a) Ethyl
2-({3-[(4-{4-[amino(imino)methyl]benzyl}-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-yl)amino]-2-benzyl-3-
oxopropanoyl}amino)acetate (10a) was prepared from ethyl
2-{[2-benzyl-3-oxo-3-({3-oxo-4-[4-(5-oxo-4,5-dihydro-
1,2,4-oxadiazol-3-yl)benzyl]-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-yl}amino)propanoyl]amino}acetate
(8a) (0.150 g, 0.250 mmol) according to the general procedure for
catalytic hydrogenation in acetic acid at room temperature; yield: 0.134
g (87 %), light brown crystals. mp 130-135 °C; IR (KBr) ν [cm-1] 3302,
2982, 1684, 1616, 1558, 1512, 1403, 1196, 1050, 700, 538. 1H NMR (DMSO-d
6) δ [ppm] 1.14 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz, Gly-OCH2CH3), 1.77 (s, 3H, AcOH),
3.01- 3.44 (m, 2H, -CHCH2Ph), 3.68 (t, 1H, J = 7.5 Hz, -CHCH2Ph), 3.82
(d, 2H, J = 5.3 Hz, Gly-αH), 4.05 (q, 2H, J= 7.0 Hz, Gly-OCH2CH3), 4.79
(s, 2H, -OCH2CON-), 5.22 (s, 2H, -CH2-(4-amidino)-Ar), 6.92 (d, 1H, J=
8.9 Hz, Ar-H5), 7.05 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 8.9 Hz, J 2 = 2.2 Hz, Ar-H6),
7.13-7.27 (m, 5H, -CHCH2Ph), 7.34 (d, 1H, J = 2.2 Hz, Ar-H8), 7.44 (d,
2H, J = 8.3 Hz, (4-amidino)-Ar-H), 7.72 (d, 2H, J = 8.3 Hz,
(4-amidino)-Ar-H), 8.60 (br s, 1H, Gly-NHCO-), 10.22 (br s, 1H, -NHCO-).
MS (FAB, m/z) 558 (MH+, 100), 323 (29), 296 (9), 154 (24), 134 (44), 91
(27), 55 (44). Anal. (C32H35N5O8 x H2O) C, H, N.
