$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for catalytic hydrogenation
The solution of the starting compound (10.0 mmol) in appropriate solvent
in the presence of palladium on activated charcoal (10 % by weight) was
stirred under hydrogen atmosphere overnight. The product was isolated by
filtration and evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure.
4-[(7-Amino-3-oxo-2,3-dihydro-4H-1,4-benzoxazin-4-yl)methyl]benzonitrile
(4) 4. Synthesis of methyl
3-[(4-{4-[amino(imino)methyl]benzyl}-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-
yl}amino]-2-benzyl-3-oxopropanoate acetate (9) Methyl
3-[(4-{4-[amino(imino)methyl]benzyl}-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2 H
-1,4-benzoxazin-7-yl}amino]-2-benzyl-3- oxopropanoate in the form of
acetate (9) was prepared from methyl
2-benzyl-3-oxo-3-({3-oxo-4-[4-(5-oxo-4,5-dihydro-
1,2,4-oxadiazol-3-yl)benzyl]-3,4-dihydro-2 H
-1,4-benzoxazin-7-yl}amino)propanoate (7) (0.261 g, 0.049 mmol) in acetic
acid according to general procedure for catalytic hydrogenation at room
temperature; yield: 0.229 g (85 %), brown crystals. mp 145-148 °C; IR
(NaCl) ν [cm-1] 3057, 1666, 1612, 1552, 1512, 1407, 1236, 1051, 814, 701.
1H NMR (DMSO-d 6) δ [ppm] 1.84 (s, 3H, AcOH), 3.09-3.12 (m, 2H,
-CHCH2Ph), 3.62 (s, 3H, -COOCH3), 3.79 (t, 1H, J = 7.5 Hz, -CHCH2Ph),
4.79 (s, 2H, -OCH2CON-), 5.22 (s, 2H, -CH2CH2-(4-amidino)-Ar), 6.92 (d,
1H, J = 8.9 Hz, Ar-H5), 7.01 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 8.9 Hz, J 2 = 2.2 Hz, Ar-H6),
7.16-7.25 (m, 5H, -CHCH2Ph), 7.28 (d, 1H, J = 2.2 Hz, Ar-H8), 7.45 (d,
2H, J = 8.1 Hz, (4-amidino)-Ar-H), 7.72 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz,
(4-amidino)-Ar-H), 10.19 (s, 1H, -CONH-). MS (FAB): m/z (%) = 487 (MH+,
100), 323 (14), 296 (10), 154 (35), 134 (36), 107 (16), 91 (25), 71 (42),
55 (48). Anal. (C27H26N4O5 x 3AcOH) C, H, N.
