$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for catalytic hydrogenation
The solution of the starting compound (10.0 mmol) in appropriate solvent
in the presence of palladium on activated charcoal (10 % by weight) was
stirred under hydrogen atmosphere overnight. The product was isolated by
filtration and evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure.
4-[(7-Amino-3-oxo-2,3-dihydro-4H-1,4-benzoxazin-4-yl)methyl]benzonitrile
(4)
(2S)-2-({3-[(4-{4-[Amino(imino)methyl]benzyl}-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-yl)amino]-2-benzyl-3-
oxopropanoyl}amino)pentanedioic acid acetate (11)
(2S)-2-({3-[(4-{4-[Amino(imino)methyl]benzyl}-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-yl)amino]-2-benzyl-3-
oxopropanoyl}amino)pentanedioic acid acetate (11) was prepared from
(2S)-2-{[2-benzyl-3-oxo-3-({3-oxo-4-[4-(5-
oxo-4,5-dihydro-1,2,4-oxadiazol-3-yl)benzyl]-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-7-
yl}amino)propanoyl]amino}pentanedioic acid (0.235 g, 0.365 mmol)
according to the general procedure for catalytic hydrogenation in acetic
acid at room temperature; yield 0.184 g (83 %), light yellow crystals. mp
177-181 °C; IR (KBr) ν [cm-1] 3330, 1678, 1615, 1512, 1403, 1221, 1050,
895, 700, 537. 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6) δ [ppm] 1.91 (s, 3H, AcOH), 1.69-1.84
(m, 2H, Glu-βH), 2.02-2.18 (m, 2H, Glu-γH), 3.03-3.16 (m, 2H,
-CHCH2CH2Ph), 3.95-4.02 (m, 1H, Glu-αH), 4.79 (s, 2H, -OCH2CON-), 5.23
(s, 2H, -CH2-(4-amidino)-Ar), 6.90 and 6.96 (2 x d, 1H, J = 7.7 Hz,
Ar-H5), 7.12-7.28 (m, 6H, -CHCH2Ph, Ar-H6), 7.46-7.51 (m, 3H,
(4-amidino)-Ar-H, H8), 7.69-7.73 (m, 2H, (4-amidino-Ar-H), 8.20 (br d,
1H, J = 8.9 Hz, Glu-CONH-), 10.21 (br s, 1H, Ar-NHCO-). MS (FAB, m/z) 602
(MH+, 16), 556 (2), 498 (3), 473 (3), 391 (17), 307 (22), 289 (12), 154
(100), 137 (75), 107 (27), 71 (56), 57 (60). Anal. calcd for C31H31N5O8 x
AcOH x H2O: 58.31 %C; 5.49 %H; 10.30 %N; found: 58.76 %C; 5.68 %H; 9.98
%N.
