$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Substituted
N-(4-Carbamimidoyl-benzyl)-[4-amino-3-oxo-morpholin-2-yl]-acetamide,
Acetic Acid Salt (13). General Procedure. 12 (1.4-8 mM) in alcoholic
solvent was treated with palladium (10% on activated carbon (Pd(C)), 100-
500 mg/mmol of 12). The solution was stirred under hydrogen gas
atmosphere for typically 1-3 h. Palladium was filtered off and the clear
solution was evaporated. Purification on preparative HPLC using aqueous
methanol with 1% of acetic acid as eluent followed by lyophilization gave
13 as a white powder.
N-(4-Amidinobenzyl)-[(R)-3-oxo-4-(3-phenyl-ureido)-morpholin-2-yl]-acetamide
Mono Acetate ((R)-13i). See general procedure. (R)-12i (8 mM) and Pd(C)
(150 mg/mmol of (R)-12i) in aqueous ethanol (88%)/THF 8:5 was
hydrogenolyzed for 2 h and purified using gradient HPLC (aqueous methanol
30-100%, 1% acetic acid) to yield (R)-13i as a white powder (0.027 g,
81%). [α]D 25 +23.8° (c 0.20 methanol); 1H NMR (methanol-d4, 300 MHz) δ
1.94 (s, 3H, acetate), 2.87 (dd, J = 15.5; 4.4 Hz, 1H), 2.92-3.07 (broad,
1H), 3.38-3.51 (m, 1H), 3.87-4.16 (m, 3H), 4.47 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H),
4.53-4.56 (broad, 1H), 4.55 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.95-7.02 (m, 1H),
7.14-7.22 (m, 2H), 7.42-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.48-7.54 (m, 2H), 7.71-7.76 (m,
2H); 13C NMR (methanol-d4, 75.5 MHz) δ 21.5 (acetate), 38.0, 42.5, 51.5,
63.3, 75.0, 120.0, 123.1, 127.1, 127.8, 127.9, 128.4, 138.8, 145.8,
156.0, 167.0, 170.3, 171.2, 177.0; HRMS m/z calcd for C21H25N6O4+ (MH+):
425.1937. Found: 425.1936. Analytical HPLC tR = 7.6 min, 99.5% pure (A),
tR = 6.7 min, 99.7% pure (B).
