$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A: Starting material (1 eq.) and sodium
acetate (2.0 eq.) were dissolved in DMSO (0.1M) and the solutionwas
flushed with dioxygen. Pd(OAc)2 (0.1 eq.) was added and the resulting
solution was stirred for 24h at 55°C.The reaction mixture was diluted
with a large volume of water and was extracted with ethyl acetate. The
combined organic layers were washed with saturated NaCl solution, dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
reaction mixture was purified by column chromatography (SiO2; Petroleum
ether/AcOEt mixture). Acetic acid
3-acetyl-7-ethanesulfonyl-2,3,3a,4,6a,7-hexahydro-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]carbazol-4-yl
ester, yield 75%. colourless oil, IR (solid, NaCl): ν = 2939, 1737, 1644,
1413, 1348, 1233, 1154, 1038, 942, 731 cm-1. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 200 MHz, T
= 383 K) major+minor products: δ (ppm) = 7.33-7.21 (m, 2H), 7.20-6.99
(m,2H), 6.16-6.12 (m, 1H), 5.92-5.981 (m, 1H), 5.46 (broad s, 1H), 4.75
(broad s, 1H), 4.0-3.80 (m, 2H), 3.61-3.45 (m, 3H), 3.38-3.12 (m, 2H),
2.45-2.20 (m, 2H), 2.02 (broad s, 3H), 1.88 (broad s, 3H), 1.26 (t, J =
7.5 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5 MHz, T = 298K): Major product: δ (ppm)
= 170.3 (Cq), 170.1 (Cq), 140.1 (Cq), 135.9 (Cq), 129.5 (CH), 128.5 (CH),
128.0 (CH), 125.2 (CH), 123.1 (CH), 114.5 (CH), 70.3 (CH), 65.2 (CH),
64.6 (CH), 51.7 (Cq), 45.3 (CH2), 42.5 (CH2), 36.7 (CH2), 22.3 (CH3),
21.0 (CH3), 7.7 (CH3). Minor product: δ (ppm) = 170.8 (Cq), 170.4 (Cq),
140.0 (Cq), 135.3 (Cq), 129.6 (CH), 129.3 (CH), 128.0 (CH), 124.5 (CH),
123.1 (CH), 114.2 (CH), 67.7 (CH), 65.3 (CH), 62.6 (CH), 50.8 (Cq), 45.4
(CH2), 43.9 (CH2), 39.3 (CH2), 22.9 (CH3), 21.1 (CH3), 7.8 (CH3). MS
(LSIMS) m/z (%): 345 [M-OAc]+ (100), 405 [M+H]+ (85), 427 [M+Na]+ (83).
HRMS (LSIMS): [M+H]+ C20H25N2O5S: calcd 405.1484; found 405.1492 (-2.2
ppm).
