$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-protected
product (3 g) was dissolved in methanol (100 mL), and 10% palladium on
charcoal (1.2 g, 50% wet) was added. The mixture was hydrogenated at 30
psi and 25 °C for 3 h. The catalyst was removed and the solvent
evaporated. The residue was purified. L-Valyl-L-Proline hexylamide
hydrogen oxalate, yield 84%. Mp 146-147 °C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, DMSO-6) δ
7.85-7.91 (1H, t, NH), 4.25-4.32 (1H, q, NCHCO of Pro), 3.93-3.96 (1H, d,
NCHCO of Val), 3.43-3.72 (2H, m, NCH2), 2.95-3.07 (2H, m, CONHCH2),
1.66-2.15 (5H, m, (CH3)2CH, NCH2CH2CH2), 1.25-1.39 (8H, m, 4 x CH2),
0.8-1.2 (6H, m, 3 x CH3). Purity (Kromasil C-18;
methanol/water/trifluoroacetic acid 50:50:0.1) 100%. MS m/z 298 [M + H]+.
Anal. (C16H31N3O2.(COOH)2) C H N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Inhibitors of Tripeptidyl Peptidase II. 3. Derivation of Butabindide by
Successive Structure Optimizations Leading to a Potential General
Approach to Designing Exopeptidase Inhibitors
