$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A. N-Protected dipeptide or amino acid
(2.9 mmol) was dissolved in tetrahydrofuran (30 mL), cooled to -10 °C,
and treated with isobutyl chloroformate (430 mg, 3.14 mmol) and
N-ethylmorpholine (360 mg, 3.14 mmol). After 30 min, amine (230 mg, 3.14
mmol) was added and the mixture stirred at room temperature overnight.
The mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (200 mL); washed successively
with dil HCl (50 mL), dil NaHCO3 (50 mL), and water; and dried (Na2SO4),
and the solvent was removed. (2S)-Aminobutyryl-(2S)-indolinecarboxylic
Acid n-Butylamide Hydrogen Oxalate, yield 80%. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CD3OD) δ
8.25 (1H, m, NH), 7.25 (4H, m, Ar CH), 5.1 (2H, m, 2 x NCHCO, obscured),
3.8 (2H, m, ArCH2), 3.5 (2H, m, CH2 of indoline), 3.2 (2H, m, NCH2), 2.0
(2H, m, CH2 of Abu), 0.9-1.8 (10H, m, CH3 of Abu, CH3CH2CH2); MS m/z 304
[M + H]+; HPLC purity(lichrosorb rp select b,
methanol/water/trifluoroacetic acid 40:60:0.1) 99.8%. Anal.
(C17H25N3O2.(COOH)2.0.75H2O) C H; N calculated 10.33, found 9.84.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Inhibitors of Tripeptidyl Peptidase II. 3. Derivation of Butabindide by
