$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-protected
product (3 g) was dissolved in methanol (100 mL), and 10% palladium on
charcoal (1.2 g, 50% wet) was added. The mixture was hydrogenated at 30
psi and 25 °C for 3 h. The catalyst was removed and the solvent
evaporated. The residue was purified. L-Valyl-L-proline
cyclohexylmethylamide hydrogen oxalate, yield 71.7%. Mp 157-158 °C. 1H
NMR (200 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.85-7.90 (1H, t, NH), 4.28-4.35 (1H, q, NCHCO
of Pro), 3.94-3.97 (1H, d, NCHCO of Val), 3.17-3.70 (2H, m, NCH2),
2.82-2.95 (2H, m, NHCH2CH), S6 1.51-2.50 (10H, m, (CH3)CH, NCH2CH2CH2 of
Pro, CH2CHCH2), 0.75-1.4 (12H, m, 2 x CH3, 3 x CH2 of cyclohexyl). MS m/z
310 [M + H]+. Purity (lichrosorb rp select b;
methanol/water/trifluoroacetic acid 70:30:0.1) 100%. Anal. (C17H31N3O2.
(COOH)2.0.25H2O) C H; N calc 9.98%, found 10.40%.
