$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-protected
product (3 g) was dissolved in methanol (100 mL), and 10% palladium on
charcoal (1.2 g, 50% wet) was added. The mixture was hydrogenated at 30
psi and 25 °C for 3 h. The catalyst was removed and the solvent
evaporated. The residue was purified.
(2S)-Aminobutyryl-4-cis-benzyl-L-proline n-butylamide Hydrogen Oxalate,
yield 25%. 1H NMR (400 MHz CD3OD) δ 7.15-7.32 (5H, m, Ar CH), 4.28-4.48
(1H, m, NCHCO), 4.10-4.22 (1H, m, NCHCO), 3.68-3.87 (1H, m, NCH(H) of
Pro), 3.06-3.42 (3H, m, NCH(H) of Pro, NCH2 of butyl), 2.44-2.84 (3H,
PhCH2, CHCH(H)CH of Pro), 2.10-2.36 (1H, m, CHCH(H)CH of Pro), 1.76-2.02
(2H, m, CH2 of Abu), 1.26-1.67 (5H, m, CH3CH2CH2, PHCH2CH), 0.86-1.12
(6H, m, 2 x CH3); MS m/z 346 [M]+; HPLC purity (Kromasil C-18,
acetonitrile/water/trifluoracetic acid 30:70:0.1) 88.9% cis isomer, 10.1%
trans isomer. Anal. (C20H31N2O2.1.25(COOH)2.0.25H2O) C H N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Inhibitors of Tripeptidyl Peptidase II. 3. Derivation of Butabindide by
