$DATUM Method 2: A suspension of compound 7 (0.24 g, 1.00 mmol) and 10% Pd/C
(24.0 mg) in MeOH (2 mL) was hydrogenated at 20 psi during 2 h (TLC
control, silica, 2% THF/CH2Cl2). The catalyst was removed by filtration
through a pad of Celite (1 x 2 cm), and to the resulting filtrate with
stirring was added DMTMM (0.33 g, 1.20 mmol) followed by addition of
(S)-2-methylbutanoic acid (153 mg, 1.50 mmol). Stirring was continued for
12 h at room temperature. The solvent was evaporated, and flash
chromatography of the residue over silica gel (3-6 cm) with 70% ethyl
acetate/hexane gave compound 1 in 89% yield. mp 106-107°C (lit.4
108-109°C); [α]20D -46.6 (c 0.88, MeOH) (lit.4 [α] D -50.1 (c 1.19,
MeOH)); IR (KBr) νmax 3279, 2965, 1730, 1687, 1644, 1545, 1150 cm-1; 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 0.93 (3H, t, J = 7.4 Hz, H-13), 1.16 (3H, d, J =
6.8 Hz, H-14), 1.47 (1H, m, H-12b), 1.68 (2H, m, H-4b, H-12a), 2.22 (1H,
m, H-11), 2.50 (1H, m, H-4a), 2.68 and 2.76 (2H, d of AB system, J = 5.2,
J = 13.2 Hz, H-5b, H-5a), 2.80 (2H, t, J = 7.6 Hz, H-8), 4.00 (2H, m,
H-7), 4.49 (1H, ddd, J = 5.2, 5.2, 13.2 Hz, H-3), 6.30 (1H, d, J = 5.2
Hz, H-9), 7.25 (5H, m, H-Ar); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 12.1 (C-13),
17.6 (C-14), 24.6 (C-4), 27.5 (C-12), 31.9 (C-5), 34.2 (C-8), 41.9 (C-7),
43.2 (C-11), 51.4 (C-3), 126.8 (C-Ar), 128.7 (2C-Ar), 129.2 (2C-Ar),
138.4 (C-Ar), 171.3 (C-6), 172.1 (C-2), 177.1 (C-10); ESIMSm/z 317.2
[M+H]+; anal. C 68.69%, H 7.33%, N 8.89%, calcd for C18H24N2O3 C 68.33%,
H 7.65%, N 8.85%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 41% overall yield over 6 steps from L-glutamic acid, alternate method
gave lower yield
