$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: o-Nosyl Removal The resin was swollen in DMF,
and after removal of the solvent a solution of β -mercaptoethanol (10
equiv) and DBU (5 equiv) in DMF was added. The suspension was agitated
for 1 h. After removal of solvent the resin was washed with DMF until the
filtrate was colourless. The procedure was repeated in steps of 30 min
until the supernatant stays colourless after the reaction. The resin was
washed with DMF. Aloc Deprotection The resin was swollen in CH2Cl2 in a
lock-up vial and N,N'-dimethylbarbituric acid (8 equiv) and Pd(PPh3)4 (10
mol%) in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL) were added. The suspension was agitated for at
least 6 h at 35 °C in the absence of light. The resin was transferred to
a glas frit and washed with a solution of sodium
diethylaminodithiocarbamate in CH2Cl2-MeOH and CH2Cl2. Compound 5c, yield
97%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD): δ = 8.50 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.39 (d, J =
8.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.74-3.64 (m, 2 H), 3.20 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 2 H), 3.17-3.03
(m, 8 H), 2.18 (tt, J1 = 7.8 Hz, J2 = 7.4 Hz, 2 H), 2.08 (tt, J1 = 7.8
Hz, J2 = 7.7 Hz, 2 H), 1.84-1.78 (m, 4 H). ESI-HRMS: m/z calcd [M + H]+:
366.2248; found: 366.2252.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Thieme chemistry journal awardees - where are they now? A convenient
route for introduction of lipophilic side chains in polyamine backbones
by solid-phase synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hahn, Frank; Schepers, Ute
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2009), (17), 2755-2760

