$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Deprotection of Cbz and 2-Cl Cbz. Cbz-protected
compound (0.64 mmol) was dissolved in EtOH (50 mL). HCl (1equiv, 0.64
mmol, 0.064 mL) and 10% Pd/C (20 wt %) were added and the mixture was
hydrogenated overnight in a Parr-apparatus at 20-50 psi. The catalyst was
filtered off and the crude product was purified by preparative HPLC.
(5S)-6-Oxo-5-[(4R)-3-oxo-4-[(phenylacetyl)amino]-3,4,5,10-tetrahydroazepino[3,4-b]indol-2(1H)-yl]-6-[(2-phenylethyl)amino]hexan-1-aminium
trifluoroacetate 14a, yield 89%. [α]20D = -54° (c 1, MeOH); IR (neat, ν,
cm-1):3257, 2935, 1776, 1630, 1144, 722; Rf (EBAW)= 0.85; MS 566 [M+1]+;
1H-NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.57-0.62 (m, 1H, CH2γ Lys), 0.89-1.03 (m, 1H,
CH2γ Lys), 1.07-1.21 (m, 2H, CH2δ), 1.25-1.41 (m, 1H, CH2δ Lys),
1.43-1.63 (m, 1H, CH2β Lys), 1.84-2.02 (m, 1H, CH2β Lys), 2.17-2.28 (m,
2H, CH2ε Lys), 2.73-2.99 (m, 3H, CH2β azep + NH), 3.22-3.38 (m, 2H,
NHCH2CH2Ph), 3.46-3.53 (m, 1H, NH), 3.34-3.59 (m, 2H, NHCH2CH2Ph), 3.70
(s, 2H, C(O)CH2Ph), 4.13 (d, 1H, J= 17.4 Hz, CH2ε azep), 4.82 (d, 1H, J=
17.5 Hz, CH2ε azep), 5.13 (dd, 1H, J1= 10.5 Hz, J2= 4.5 Hz, CHα Lys),
5.36 (dd, 1H, J1= 12.7 Hz, J2= 4.3 Hz, CHα azep), 6.99-7.38 (m, 14H, CH
arom); 13C-NMR (63MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.0 ( CH2γ Lys ), 27.0 (CH2δ Lys), 28.0
(CH2β Lys), 29.9 (CH2β azep), 37.0 (NHCH2CH2Ph), 40.0 (CH2ε Lys), 42.0
(CH2ε azep), 42.5 (NHCH2CH2Ph), 43.5 (C(O)CH2Ph) 52.0 (CHα azep), 58.0
(CHα Lys), 108.0-140.0 (CH arom + C arom), 173.0 (C(O)NHCH2CH2Ph), 175.0
(C(O)CH2Ph), 177.0 (C=O azep).
