$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4-(pyrrolidin-1-yl)piperidin-1-yl)(4-(4-(pyrrolidin-1-yl)piperidin-1-yl)phenyl)methanone
(9): Compound 9 was prepared from
4-bromo-N-((4-(pyrrolidinyl)piperidinyl)benzamide, a previously reported
compound.3 A mixture of 4-bromo-N-((4-(pyrrolidinyl)piperidinyl)benzamide
(150 mg, 0.45 mmol), 2-
Dicyclohexylphosphino-2′,4′,6′-triisopropylbiphenyl (XPhos) (106 mg, 50
mol%), tris(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium(0) (102 mg, 25 mol%), and
sodium tert-butoxide (64 mg, 0.67 mmol) in anhydrous toluene (3 mL) was
added to a sealable reaction tube. The solution was degassed with N2 for
20 minutes and 4-(1-pyrrolidinyl)piperidine (96 mg, 0.62 mmol) was added
subsequently. The reaction tube was tightly sealed and the reaction was
stirred at 120 °C for 15 hours. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, diluted with CH2Cl2, and filtered over a thick pad of celite
which was subsequently washed with CH2Cl2. The CH2Cl2 was removed by
rotary evaporation. The crude mixture was brought up in a small amount of
a methanol-water mixture and filtered. The resulting filtrate was
purified by reverse phase HPLC and the solvents were removed. 237 mg
(83%) of the TFA salt of 9 as a dark red solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ
7.40-7.34 (m, 2H), 7.10-7.603 (m, 2H), 4.70 - 4.07 (bs, 2H), 4.03-3.93
(m, 2H), 3.75-3.58 (m, 4H), 3.42 (tt, J = 12.2, 4.3 Hz, 1H), 3.35 (tt, J
= 12.2, 4.3 Hz, 1H), 3.26 - 2.95 (m, 6H), 2.90 (td, J = 13.4, 2.3 Hz,
2H), 2.29 - 1.93 (m, 12H), 1.81 (qd, J = 12.3, 4.1 Hz, 2H), 1.66 (qd, J =
12.4, 4.5 Hz, 2H). HPLC: 99%, t R 1.43 min. MS (ESI+): 411.4 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used, conversion to TFA salt during reverse phase HPLC
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Small-Molecule Ligands of Methyl-Lysine Binding Proteins: Optimization of
Selectivity for L3MBTL3
