$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Deprotection of Cbz
and 2-Cl Cbz. Cbz-protected compound (0.64 mmol) was dissolved in EtOH
(50 mL). HCl (1equiv, 0.64 mmol, 0.064 mL) and 10% Pd/C (20 wt %) were
added and the mixture was hydrogenated overnight in a Parr-apparatus at
20-50 psi. The catalyst was filtered off and the crude product was
purified by preparative HPLC.
(5R)-6-(Benzylamino)-6-oxo-5-[(4R)-3-oxo-4-[(phenylacetyl)amino]-3,4,5,10-tetrahydroazepino[3,4-b]indol-2(1H)-yl]hexan-1-aminium
trifluoroacetate 18, yield 74%. [α]20D = -14° (c 1, MeOH); IR (neat, ν,
cm-1): 3054, 2934, 2364, 2070, 1787, 1630, 1453; Rf (EBAW) 0.64; MS 552
[M+1]; 1H-NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.22-1.40 (m, 2H, CH2γ Lys), 1.50-1.64
(m, 2H, CH2δ Lys), 1.80-1.96 (m, 1H, CH2β), 2.77 (t, 2H, J= 7.2 Hz, CH2ε
Lys), 2.91 (t, 1H, J= 13.8 Hz, CH2β azep), 3.12 (dd, 1H, J1= 15.4 Hz, J2=
4.4 Hz, CH2β azep), 3.25-3.28 (m, 1H, NH), 3.61 (s, 2H, C(O)CH2Ph), 3.88
(d, J= 14.9 Hz, NHCH2Ph), 4.16 (d, J= 14.8 Hz, NHCH2Ph), 4.51 (d, 1H, J=
17.0 Hz, CH2ε azep), 4.87-4.95 (m, 1H, CH2ε azep), 5.07-5.16 (m, 1H, CHα
Lys + CHα azep), 6.51-7.37 (m, 14H, CH arom); 13C-NMR (63MHz, CDCl3) δ
24.1 (CH2γ Lys), 27.9 (CH2β Lys or CH2β azep), 28.1 (CH2β Lys or CH2β
azep), 29.1 (CH2δ Lys), 41.2 (CH2ε azep or CH2ε Lys), 41.3 (CH2ε azep or
CH2ε Lys), 43.7 (NHCH2Ph), 44.4 (C(O)CH2Ph), 52.7 (CHα azep), 57.9 (CHα
Lys), 109.1-139.4 (CH arom + C arom), 172.1 (C(O)NHBn), 174.6
(C(O)CH2Ph), 175.5 (C=O azep).
