$DATUM H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(NH)NH2•2TFA (23). Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (148mg,
0.31mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL) containing a catalytic amount of
10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under H2 atmosphere (35psi) for 18
hours. The solution was then filtered through celite and the filtrate was
concentrated. To the crude residue was added
1-H-pyrazole-1-[N,N’-bis(tert-butoxycarbonyl)]carboxamidine16 (144mg,
0.46mmol) in dissolved in DMF (3mL) containing DIPEA (0.081mL, 0.46
mmol). The solution was stirred for 18h at 35°C. The concentrated residue
22 was then directly dissolved and stirred in 1.0M HCl/AcOH (4mL) at room
temperature for 18 hours. The residue was concentrated and purified by
reverse phase chromatography and lyophilized to yield 23 as a white solid
(42 mg, 27% yield). Both cis and trans isomers visible by NMR but only
the major isomer was reported. MH+ 396.1H NMR (CD3OD) δ 2.36 (s, 6H),
2.55 (dd, 1H), 2.90 (dd, 1H), 3.00 (d, 1H), 3.14 (m, 3H), 3.49 (t, 1H),
4.30 (m, 1H), 4.49 (br s, 1H), 4.62 (m, 1H), 6.50, 6.53 (2s, 2H), 6.71
(m, 1H), 7.20 (m, 3H). Calc(%): C, 47.21; H, 4.60; N, 10.12. Found(%): C,
47.13; H, 4.51; N, 10.33. HPLC gradient IV, HPLC K’: 7.22.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel C-Terminus Modifications of the Dmt-Tic Motif: A New Class of
Dipeptide Analogues Showing Altered Pharmacological Profiles Toward the
Opioid Receptors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
