$DATUM H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(O)NHEt•TFA (27). Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (120mg,
0.25mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL) containing a catalytic amount of
10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under H2 atmosphere (35psi) for 18
hours. The solution was then filtered through celite and the filtrate was
concentrated. The crude product was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (5mL) containing
a few drops of TEA and ethyl isocyanate (0.024mL, 0.30mmol). The solution
was stirred at room temperature for 1h. The reaction was quenched by
addition of MeOH and the solvent was concentrated. The crude residue was
dissolved and stirred in 1.0M HCl/AcOH (3mL) at room temperature for 1h.
The product was purified by reverse phase chromatography and lyophilized.
dipeptide 27 as a white solid (33 mg, 25% yield). Both cis and trans
isomer visible by NMR, major isomer reported. MH+ 425. 1H NMR (CD3OD) δ
1.05 (t, 3H), 2.23 (br s, 6H), 2.72 (dd, 2H), 2.93 (dd, 1H), 3.06 (m,
5H), 3.21 (t, 1H), 3.48 (d, 1H), 4.26 (d, 1H), 4.56 (dd, 1H), 4.76 (dd,
1H), 6.20 (s, 2H), 6.71 (d, 1H), 7.04 (t, 2H), 7.08 (t, 1H). Calc(%): C,
53.64; H, 5.75; N, 9.27. Found(%): C, 53.63; H, 5.83; N, 9.21. HPLC
gradient II, HPLC K’: 5.31.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel C-Terminus Modifications of the Dmt-Tic Motif: A New Class of
Dipeptide Analogues Showing Altered Pharmacological Profiles Toward the
Opioid Receptors
