$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(O)NHEt•TFA (27).
Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (120mg, 0.25mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL)
containing a catalytic amount of 10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under
H2 atmosphere (35psi) for 18 hours. The solution was then filtered
through celite and the filtrate was concentrated. The crude product was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (5mL) containing a few drops of TEA and ethyl
isocyanate (0.024mL, 0.30mmol). The solution was stirred at room
temperature for 1h. The reaction was quenched by addition of MeOH and the
solvent was concentrated. The crude residue was dissolved and stirred in
1.0M HCl/AcOH (3mL) at room temperature for 1h. The product was purified
by reverse phase chromatography and lyophilized. dipeptide 27 as a white
solid (33 mg, 25% yield). H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(O)NHadam•TFA (30). Similar
procedure used as for dipeptide 27 using 1-adamatyl isocyanate (25%
yield). Only one cis/trans isomer visible by NMR. MH+ 531. 1H NMR (CD3OD)
δ 1.74 (s, 6H), 2.00 (s, 6H), 2.08 (s, 3H), 2.24 (s, 6H), 2.33 (d, 1H),
2.37 (s, 1H), 2.39 (d, 1H), 2.42 (d, 1H), 3.10 (dd, 2H), 3.24 (t, 1H),
3.38 (m, 1H), 4.37 (d, 1H), 4.66 (d, 1H), 6.43 (s, 2H), 7.01 (d, 1H),
7.13 (d, 1H),7.19 (m, 2H). Calc(%): C, 52.87; H, 5.56; N, 6.63. Found(%):
C, 52.76; H, 5.43; N, 7.08. HPLC gradient I, HPLC K’: 3.48.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel C-Terminus Modifications of the Dmt-Tic Motif: A New Class of
