$DATUM H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(NH)CH3•2TFA (21). Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (124mg,
0.26mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL) containing a catalytic amount of
10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under H2 atmosphere (35psi) for 18
hours. The solution was then filtered through celite and the filtrate was
concentrated. To the crude residue 18 (MH+ 454) was added methyl
acetimidate hydrochloride (141mg, 1.29mmol) dissolved in DMF (3mL)
containing TEA (0.216mL, 1.55mmol). The solution was stirred at room
temperature for 24h. The solution was concentrated and the residue was
dissolved and stirred in 1.0M HCl/AcOH (4mL) for 18h at room temperature.
The concentrated residue was then purified by reverse phase
chromatography and lyophilized to afford 21 as a white solid (28 mg, 21%
yield). Both cis and trans isomers visible by NMR but only the major
isomer was reported. MH+ 395.1H NMR (CD3OD) δ 2.25 (s, 3H), 2.33 (s,
6H),2.64 (dd, 1H), 2.84 (dd, 1H), 3.10 (d, 1H), 3.18 (dd, 1H), 3.24 (dd,
1H), 3.50 (d, 1H),4.30 (d, 1H), 4.57 (m, 1H), 4.63 (m, 1H), 6.51 (s, 2H),
6.69 (d, 1H), 7.20 (m, 3H). Calc(%): C, 47.29; H, 4.75; N, 7.71.
Found(%): C, 47.35; H, 4.74; N, 7.65. HPLC gradient IV, HPLC K’: 6.97.
