$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N(Me)2•2TFA (24).
Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (104mg, 0.22mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL)
containing a catalytic amount of 10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under
H2 atmosphere (35psi) for 18 hours. The solution was then filtered
through celite and the filtrate was concentrated. Formaldehyde (37%wt/v)
(0.5mL, excess) was added to the crude residue in MeOH (1mL) containing
AcOH (1 drop). The solution was stirred 15min at 0°C. NaCNBH3 (54mg,
0.86mmol) was added and the solution was stirred at room temperature for
45 minutes. The solution was quenched with satd NaHCO3 (10mL) and
extracted (3X) with EtOAc. The organic layer was dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated. The residue (MH+ 482) was then stirred in 1.0M HCl/AcOH 24h
at room temperature. The product was purified by reverse phase
chromatography and lyophilized.Both cis and trans isomers visible by NMR
but only the major isomer was reported. H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHBn•2TFA (25).
Similar procedure used as for dipeptide 24 using benzaldehyde (20%
yield). Both cis and trans isomers visible by NMR but only the major
isomer was reported. MH+ 444. 1H NMR (CD3OD) δ 2.24 (s, 6H), 2.61 (dd,
1H), 2.68 (dd, 1H), 2.99 (m, 1H), 3.15 (dd, 1H), 3.25 (d, 1H), 4.06 (d,
1H), 4.23 (dd, 2H), 4.33 (d, 1H), 4.60 (dd, 1H), 4.95 (m, 1H), 5.17 (d,
1H), 6.50 (s, 2H), 6.77 (d, 1H), 7.19 (m, 3H), 7.38 (s, 2H), 7.48 (s,
3H). Calc(%): C, 52.85; H, 4.97; N, 5.57. Found(%): C, 52.87; H, 4.92; N,
5.66. HPLC gradient II, HPLC K’: 4.96.
