$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(O)CH3•TFA (33).
Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (44mg, 0.092mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL)
containing a catalytic amount of 10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under
H2 atmosphere (35psi) at room temperature for 18h. The solution was
filtered through celite and concentrated. To the crude residue (MH+ 454)
in CH2Cl2 (3mL) was added DIPEA (0.019mL, 0.11mmol) along with acetyl
chloride (0.08mL, 0.110mmol) at 0°C. Solution was stirred for 10min at
0oC, then 30min at room temperature. The solution was quenched by
addition of MeOH, diluted with CH2Cl2 (20mL) and washed with satd NaHCO3,
5% KHSO4 and brine. The organic layer was dried (Na2SO4), and
concentrated. The residue was dissolved in 1.0M HCl/AcOH (2mL) and
stirred at room temperature for 1h. The solution was concentrated and the
product was purified by reverse phase chromatography and lyophilized. 33
as a white solid (23mg, 50% yield). H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2NHC(O)Ph•TFA (34).
Similar procedure used as for dipeptide 33 using benzoyl chloride (20%
yield). Only one cis/trans isomer visible by NMR. MH+ 458. 1H NMR (CD3OD)
δ 1.74 (dd, 1H), 2.21 (s, 6H), 2.42 (d, 1H), 2.77 (dd, 1H), 3.15 (dd,
1H), 3.25 (d, 1H), 3.47 (dd, 1H), 3.55 (m, 1H), 4.42 (d, 1H), 4.75 (d,
1H), 5.17 (dd, 1H), 6.39 (s, 2H), 7.07 (d, 1H), 7.16 (d, 1H), 7.21 (m,
2H), 7.50 (t, 2H), 7.58 (t, 1H), 7.81 (d, 2H). Calc(%): C, 59.43; H,
5.49; N, 6.79. Found(%): C, 59.36; H, 5.50; N, 6.68. HPLC gradient II,
HPLC K’: 6.55.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel C-Terminus Modifications of the Dmt-Tic Motif: A New Class of
Dipeptide Analogues Showing Altered Pharmacological Profiles Toward the
Opioid Receptors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
