$DATUM H-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N(Me)2•2TFA (24). Boc-L-Dmt-L-Tic-CH2N3 (16) (104mg,
0.22mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (8mL) containing a catalytic amount of
10% Pd/C. The solution was shaken under H2 atmosphere (35psi) for 18
hours. The solution was then filtered through celite and the filtrate was
concentrated. Formaldehyde (37%wt/v) (0.5mL, excess) was added to the
crude residue in MeOH (1mL) containing AcOH (1 drop). The solution was
stirred 15min at 0°C. NaCNBH3 (54mg, 0.86mmol) was added and the solution
was stirred at room temperature for 45 minutes. The solution was quenched
with satd NaHCO3 (10mL) and extracted (3X) with EtOAc. The organic layer
was dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated. The residue (MH+ 482) was then
stirred in 1.0M HCl/AcOH 24h at room temperature. The product was
purified by reverse phase chromatography and lyophilized.Both cis and
trans isomers visible by NMR but only the major isomer was reported.
dipeptide 24 as a white solid (16 mg, 15% yield). MH+ 382. 1H NMR (CD3OD)
δ 2.14 (br s, 1H), 2.28 (d, 1H), 2.36 (s, 6H), 2.75 (dd, 1H), 2.86 (dd,
1H), 2.93 (s, 6H), 3.06 (dd, 1H), 3.17 (dd, 1H), 3.60 (d, 1H), 4.45 (d,
1H), 4.64 (dd, 1H), 4.95 (m, 1H), 6.53 (s, 2H), 6.84 (d, 1H), 7.22 (m,
3H). Calc(%): C, 49.47; H, 5.32; N, 6.23. Found(%): C, 49.42; H, 5.26; N,
6.35. HPLC gradient II, HPLC K’: 3.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel C-Terminus Modifications of the Dmt-Tic Motif: A New Class of
Dipeptide Analogues Showing Altered Pharmacological Profiles Toward the
Opioid Receptors
